    {
      "title": "French education minister says up to 500 schools will remain partially or fully closed on Monday after student protests – Europe live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/04/friedrich-merz-german-chancellor-ukraine-kyiv-russia-strikes-war-zelenskyy-putin-europe-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>At least 5,000 people, mainly teenagers, have been arrested while dozens of people, including students and teachers, have been injured</p><p>Germany is Ukraine’s largest donor and has sent Kyiv more than €43.3 billion ($48.8 billion) since the war began, along with equipment and weapons.<br /><br />\n Zelenskyy thanked Merz for visiting the Ukrainian capital describing him as “A leader of a country that consistently demonstrates leadership in protecting the lives of Ukrainians from Russian strikes. <br /><br />\n We are grateful for all the support, and today we are preparing decisions to give us in Ukraine, and all of Europe, greater capabilities to defend ourselves. There will be important agreements between Ukraine and Germany. Russia must be stopped together.”<br /></p><p>Zelenskyy in the past hour has been tweeting about the strikes and the German chancellor’s visit, thanking Merz for his support.<br /><br />\n On the Kyiv strike this morning he confirmed it had been a drone on the Northern Bridge (Pivnichnyi Bridge).<br /><br />\n He noted too a drone attack on a pharmaceutical warehouse in Sumy which killed one person and a strike on a communications facility in Dnipro.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/04/friedrich-merz-german-chancellor-ukraine-kyiv-russia-strikes-war-zelenskyy-putin-europe-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-04T14:35:31"
    },
    {
      "title": "Russia strikes Kyiv bridge as German chancellor visits Ukraine in show of support",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/04/russia-strikes-kyiv-bridge-german-chancellor-merz-visits-ukraine",
      "description": "<p>Attack happened shortly after Friedrich Merz arrived in city, on unannounced visit intended to underline Germany’s backing</p><p>Russia has struck another major bridge in Kyiv as the German chancellor, Friedrich Merz, arrived in the capital in a show of support for Ukraine.</p><p>A Russian drone hit Kyiv’s key Northern Bridge over the Dnipro River, marking the fourth consecutive day that Russia has targeted bridges used by thousands of residents commuting between the city’s two banks. Video footage showed cars driving across the bridge as the drone plunged into the roadway and exploded in a burst of fire. Two people were injured in the strike, said Kyiv’s mayor, Vitali Klitschko.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/04/russia-strikes-kyiv-bridge-german-chancellor-merz-visits-ukraine\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-04T11:53:09"
    },
    {
