    {
      "title": "Germany's Merz visits Kyiv as Russia steps up attacks on Ukrainian cities",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/germany-s-merz-visits-kyiv-as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-cities-126100400245_1.html",
      "description": "German Chancellor Friedrich Merz arrived in Kyiv Sunday in a show of support as Russia intensifies its attacks on Ukrainian cities.\nThe aerial war has intensified, with Moscow menacing cities across Ukraine with hard-to-intercept ballistic missiles and jet-powered drones, while Kyiv has been striking Russia's oil industry and businesses.\nMerz said he travelled to Kyiv, his second trip as chancellor, to demonstrate Germany's support for Ukraine.\n\"If Russia is not stopped, its war machine will sooner or later turn against us,\" he said in a statement Sunday, adding that he told Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy, \"You can continue to count on our help.\"\nMerz said the partnership between the two countries was \"not a one-way street,\" pointing to German and Ukrainian companies jointly developing technologies that benefit both sides. \"This makes us safer and stronger,\" he said.\nUkrainian Foreign Minister Andrii Sybiha said the agenda would focus on \"strengthening Ukraine, our defenc",
